  "functionalScope": "Three source reconstruction families now build exact participant DATA without overwriting source stores. Independent-delivery covers all four native lane combinations after actual failed pending saves and genuine older cold reopen, preserving nonempty queued suggestions/decisions, revisions, version packets, relay receipts, immutable native versions and future document/comment Undo/Redo. Actual live writer exclusion, absent-only participant recovery and repeated cold recovery are exercised. Native-valid missing/changed queue rows require reconciliation. Ordered native version prefixes are checked beyond legacy set membership. Both independent builders require an exact complete LIVE wrapper round-trip, preventing silent loss or relabeling of identity/binding/unknown metadata. Complete parent plans and retained cut references/digests are re-admitted. The genuine current seven-member native/whole-upload preflight and all prior read cancellation guards remain required.",
  "boundary": "Private DATA/participant recovery, not an editable room, native union, writer retirement, source-write acknowledgement, server-finalized review decision, credential or authenticated activation. Existing original protocol formats, default actor policies, Rust/WASM bytes, package/model versions and thirteen V1 gates remain unchanged. Controlled storage/locks do not establish physical power-loss durability.",
